Introduction – SAP CPI Consultant
----------------------------------
Hi, my name is Srinivas. I have 7 years of experience in the IT industry, with the last 3 years focused on SAP Cloud Platform Integration (CPI).
I specialize in designing and developing end-to-end integrations between SAP and non-SAP systems, both cloud and on-premise.
I have hands-on experience with iFlow development using tools like Groovy scripting, XSLT/JSON transformations, and graphical message mapping.

I’ve worked on integration scenarios involving systems like S/4HANA, SuccessFactors, Concur, Salesforce, and Ariba, using a wide range of adapters
such as SFTP, HTTP, SOAP, OData, IDoc, JDBC, Mail, AS2, and SuccessFactors Adapter.

My key responsibilities include:
===============================

Designing, developing, and deploying integration flows in SAP CPI.
Using key integration patterns: Content Modifier, Router, Splitter/Gather, Enricher, Exception Handling, and ProcessDirect.
Handling dynamic configurations, secure authentication (OAuth, Basic Auth, Client Certs), and modular integration design.
Promoting artifacts across landscapes using TMS.
Monitoring and troubleshooting through CPI Monitor, Logs, and Trace.
I follow best practices for reusability, performance, and error handling. I'm passionate about clean integration design and
continuously stay updated with the latest SAP technologies and integration trends.

I’m passionate about clean and scalable integration design, and I always focus on optimizing performance and
ensuring smooth monitoring and exception handling. I stay updated with SAP’s latest integration innovations
and best practices to bring added value to the projects I work on.